<?xml version='1.0' standalone='yes'?>
<PLUGIN name="zfs.snapsync" author="Adnan Nashawaty" version="__VERSION__" icon="zfs-snapsync.png" pluginURL="__BASE_URL__/zfs.snapsync.plg" support="https://github.com/adnanklink/zfssnapsync-unraid/issues" min="6.12.0" launch="Settings/ZFSSnapSync">Plain-English ZFS snapshot scheduling, retention cleanup, and low-space protection for Unraid.
  <CHANGES>
### __VERSION__ (__BUILD_DATE__)
- Show automatic snapshot section fields directly, without redundant dropdowns.
- Align snapshot actions and pagination, and remove empty space above the snapshot list.
- Separate Automatic snapshots, Snapshots and Backup copies, with utilities in Settings and compatible legacy links.
- Guide setup through focused steps and edit saved configuration by section; return from shared connection settings to the preserved job draft.
- Compact snapshot browsing, centered dialogs and task-based Overview summaries retain cleanup and recovery safeguards.
- Improve laptop/mobile layouts and preserve saved configuration when scheduler application fails.
- Save replication jobs directly; save shared settings independently without applying unrelated drafts.
- Compact Automation setup with a runtime summary, shown-dataset selection and persistent save controls.
- Contextual snapshot actions and consistent Send/Restore dialogs preserve existing cleanup reviews and safety checks.
- Keep the WebGUI and installer connection running while completing activation.
- Activate explicitly after package replacement, even when the package manager skips its hook.
- Avoid duplicate activation and verify the running coordinator before reporting success.
- Safely retry installations left in maintenance after a failed hook.
- Display preflight and activation errors in Unraid, and retain the original failure reason.
- Detect coordinator compatibility and explain unavailable recovery and job logs.
- Refresh only when attempts finish; refuse busy updates before package replacement and verify activation.
- Show expandable replication stages and dataset pages, with explicit loading errors and retry.
- Show job-specific logs and retain original ZFS errors with clear failure explanations and next actions.
- Add reviewed recovery for interrupted local replication, resuming original snapshots without creating fresh ones.
- Direct repeated Run Now to recovery and check interrupted receivers before creating source snapshots.
- Keep recovery reviews and diagnostic history in RAM; label shared logs separately.
- Add source retention for native local replication: new jobs default to three checkpoints; existing jobs require review before enabling cleanup.
- Run source cleanup only after verified replication, preserving receiver bases, recovery references, holds, clones and foreign snapshots.
- Add reversible Needs attention dismissal without releasing recovery protections or deleting history.
- Keep waiting transfers steady during resource checks and prevent operation status updates from shifting the page.
- Reduce snapshot inventory rescans and improve bounded loading for larger datasets.
- Correct workflow navigation and add persistent replication schedule Pause/Resume controls.
- Refresh cached Activity scripts and stabilize Details log scrolling.
- Strengthen long-text containment and refresh cached workspace styles after updates.
- Fix overflowing dataset text and preserve log drawer scrolling during refresh.
- Saved replication jobs update immediately; Activity shows native transfer progress, speed and phases.
- Fix overlapping fields and help text in the replication job editor.
- Install, update, and support URLs now use the renamed zfssnapsync-unraid repository.
- Align Activity and Automation controls; shorten the optional tab to SnapSync.
- Install and updates now track main; existing SnapSync clients can update normally.
- New SnapSync logo and plugin icons; optional Unraid navigation tab under Tools → Interface.
- Update SnapSync author attribution and add an optional developer support link.
- Fix indefinite Browse loading and add prominent dataset discovery status with retry.
- Align Refresh datasets and move tuning defaults to compact bottom controls.
- Standalone ZFS SnapSync identity, configuration, runtime paths and update manifest.
- Independent default snapshot prefixes and manual hold tag; no automatic import of original plugin work.
- Coordinator-owned deletion and batch journals with verified cancellation and RAM-only runtime history.
- Native local scheduled replication and Run Now with measured space approval and verified completion.
- Opt-in per-job retention anchor cleanup preserves the keep-all window and protected checkpoints.
- Testing build: native SSH, shared cleanup ownership and broader release gates remain unfinished.
- Stop original-plugin work and disable its schedules before using the same datasets; configuration is not imported.

  </CHANGES>

  <DESCRIPTION>
ZFS SnapSync adds plain-English scheduling and safe snapshot lifecycle management for Unraid. It keeps recent snapshots, consolidates older ones by day/week, and cleans up for low-space pressure using your configured prefix safeguards.
  </DESCRIPTION>

  <SUPPORT>https://github.com/adnanklink/zfssnapsync-unraid/issues</SUPPORT>

  <FILE Name="/boot/config/plugins/zfs.snapsync/zfs-snapsync-__VERSION__-noarch-1.txz" Min="6.12.0">
    <URL>__BASE_URL__/zfs-snapsync-__VERSION__-noarch-1.txz</URL>
    <MD5>__PKG_MD5__</MD5>
  </FILE>

  <FILE Run="/bin/bash">
    <INLINE><![CDATA[
# Unraid forwards stdout from inline scripts to the WebGUI, not stderr.
exec 2>&1
set -Eeuo pipefail
INSTALL_STAGE='initializing installation'
install_failed() {
  local status="$?"
  trap - ERR
  echo "ERROR: ZFS SnapSync installation failed while ${INSTALL_STAGE} (exit ${status})."
  echo 'The preceding message gives the blocker. Existing work must finish before installation can continue.'
  exit "$status"
}
trap install_failed ERR

PKG_DIR="/boot/config/plugins/zfs.snapsync"
PKG_FILE="zfs-snapsync-__VERSION__-noarch-1.txz"
PKG_PATH="${PKG_DIR}/${PKG_FILE}"
PKG_URL="__BASE_URL__/${PKG_FILE}"
PKG_MD5="__PKG_MD5__"
PKG_NAME="zfs-snapsync"

if command -v upgradepkg >/dev/null 2>&1; then
  UPGRADEPKG="$(command -v upgradepkg)"
elif [[ -x /sbin/upgradepkg ]]; then
  UPGRADEPKG="/sbin/upgradepkg"
elif [[ -x /usr/sbin/upgradepkg ]]; then
  UPGRADEPKG="/usr/sbin/upgradepkg"
else
  echo "ERROR: upgradepkg not found on system." >&2
  exit 1
fi

mkdir -p "${PKG_DIR}"

download_pkg() {
  if command -v wget >/dev/null 2>&1; then
    wget --no-cache -O "${PKG_PATH}" "${PKG_URL}"
  else
    curl -fsSL "${PKG_URL}" -o "${PKG_PATH}"
  fi
}

verify_md5() {
  if command -v md5sum >/dev/null 2>&1; then
    echo "${PKG_MD5}  ${PKG_PATH}" | md5sum -c -
  else
    [[ "$(md5 -q "${PKG_PATH}")" == "${PKG_MD5}" ]]
  fi
}

INSTALL_STAGE='downloading the package'
if [[ ! -f "${PKG_PATH}" ]]; then
  download_pkg
fi

INSTALL_STAGE='verifying the package checksum'
if ! verify_md5; then
  rm -f "${PKG_PATH}"
  download_pkg
  verify_md5
fi

INSTALL_STAGE='acquiring the installation lock'
echo 'Checking installation ownership…'
# Serialize installers and extract the incoming lifecycle code before replacement.
mkdir -p /var/run/zfs-snapsync-coordinator
exec 9>/var/run/zfs-snapsync-coordinator/install.lock
flock -n 9 || { echo 'Another installation is running.' >&2; exit 1; }
INSTALL_STAGE='staging the incoming package in RAM'
STAGED="$(mktemp -d /tmp/zfs-snapsync-install.XXXXXX)"
trap 'rm -rf "$STAGED"' EXIT
tar -xJf "$PKG_PATH" -C "$STAGED"
INSTALL_STAGE='checking coordinator and worker ownership before replacement'
echo 'Checking whether existing work has finished…'
php "$STAGED/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/zfs.snapsync/php/coordinator-lifecycle.php" prepare

INSTALL_STAGE='installing the package and running its activation hook'
echo 'Idle preflight passed; installing the package…'
ZFSAS_DEFER_ACTIVATION=1 "${UPGRADEPKG}" --install-new "${PKG_PATH}"

INSTALL_STAGE='verifying package registration'
if ! ls -1 /var/log/packages 2>/dev/null | grep -q "^${PKG_NAME}"; then
  echo "Package registration missing after install; retrying with --reinstall." >&2
  ZFSAS_DEFER_ACTIVATION=1 "${UPGRADEPKG}" --install-new --reinstall "${PKG_PATH}"
fi

if ! ls -1 /var/log/packages 2>/dev/null | grep -q "^${PKG_NAME}"; then
  echo "ERROR: ${PKG_NAME} is still missing from /var/log/packages after install." >&2
  exit 1
fi

INSTALL_STAGE='running package activation explicitly'
echo 'Activating the installed package…'
/bin/bash /usr/local/emhttp/plugins/zfs.snapsync/scripts/post-install.sh
INSTALL_STAGE='verifying coordinator activation'
# Some package managers ignore doinst.sh failures. Verify activation explicitly.
php /usr/local/emhttp/plugins/zfs.snapsync/php/coordinator-lifecycle.php verify
    ]]></INLINE>
  </FILE>

  <FILE Run="/bin/bash" Method="remove">
    <INLINE><![CDATA[
set -euo pipefail

if [ -x /usr/local/emhttp/plugins/zfs.snapsync/scripts/pre-remove.sh ]; then
  /usr/local/emhttp/plugins/zfs.snapsync/scripts/pre-remove.sh || true
fi

removepkg zfs-snapsync >/dev/null 2>&1 || true

# Fallback cleanup for installs that missed package DB registration.
rm -f /usr/local/sbin/zfs_snapsync
rm -rf /usr/local/emhttp/plugins/zfs.snapsync

rm -f /boot/config/plugins/zfs.snapsync/zfs-snapsync-*-noarch-1.txz
rm -f /boot/config/plugins/zfs.snapsync/zfs-snapsync-*-noarch-1.txz.md5
rmdir /boot/config/plugins/zfs.snapsync 2>/dev/null || true
    ]]></INLINE>
  </FILE>
</PLUGIN>
